FaceEvalString
	Also known as: eval_string
	
	Synopsis:
	        int FaceEvalString( Widget w, String *str, Pointer param )
	
	Description:
	
	Interpret the FACE script whose text is in str, a character string, e. g. "i =
	1; " and return -1 if the script was incorrect. Execution of an incorrect
	script causes an error message to be sent to stderr. This function is not
	available in the library libFm_c. a. widget is the reference widget, i. e. ,
	the widget which determines the content of self and of parent. It need not be
	otherwise related to the script being evaluated unless it is directly
	referenced by the script. param is any parameter. It has been declared here as
	an int but could be any legal FACE type. In a FACE script, this parameter is
	referenced by the read-only variable $.
	
	Scope: FACE scripts application 	
	
	Example:
	
	eval_string ( self, "st = WidgetName ( parent.PB_2 ) ;
	printf ( `%s\n', st ) ;", Pointer ( 2 )  ) ;
	
	The corresponding C function is: FaceEvalString
	

FaceInitTimer
	Also known as: init_timer
	
	Synopsis:
	        Timer FaceInitTimer( Widget widget, String script, None call_data, Int delay, Int repeat )
	
	Description:
	
	This function will interrupt a FACE script after a specific delay. You may
	optionally request that the script be repeated at regular intervals after its
	initial execution. It returns an identifier that you can give to FaceStopTimer
	to stop the timer. FaceInitTimer is not available in the library libFm_c. a.
	widget is the widget that will be used as "self" when the timer script is run.
	script is a string containing the script to execute. call_data is the value of
	the call_data ($) in the script. delay is the delay in milliseconds before the
	script is run. repeat if non-zero, is the delay in milliseconds between
	successive calls of the script after the initial delay.
	
	Scope: FACE scripts application 	
	
	The corresponding C function is: FaceInitTimer
	See also:
	        FaceStopTimer
	        XtAddTimeOut
	
	

FaceSetValues
	Also known as: SetValues
	
	Synopsis:
	        Int FaceSetValues( Widget w, Int num_resources, String resource1, None value1, String resource2, None value2, ... )
	
	Description:
	
	Set multiple resource values in one call to XtSetValues. num_resources
	specifies the number of resources to be set. A maximum of 5 resources can be
	set simultaneously. resource1 is the name of the first resource. value1 is the
	value to which it will be set. The values must be given in their internal form,
	not in their String form. The internal form of a resource can be obtained by
	using ConvertString.
	
	Scope: FACE scripts application 	
	
	Example:
	
	Set the resources for the scale widget in a float resource editing box:
	SetValues ( parent.scale, 3, 
	        "minimum", cftoi ( min * 100.0 ) , 
	        "maximum", cftoi ( max * 100.0 ) , 
	        "value", cftoi ( v * 100.0 )  ) ; 
	
	The corresponding C function is: FaceSetValues
	See also:
	        ConvertString
	        XtSetValue
	
	

