init_timer
	Also known as: FaceInitTimer
	
	Synopsis:
	        Timer FaceInitTimer( Widget widget, String script, None call_data, Int delay, Int repeat )
	
	Description:
	
	This function will interrupt a FACE script after a specific delay. You may
	optionally request that the script be repeated at regular intervals after its
	initial execution. It returns an identifier that you can give to FaceStopTimer
	to stop the timer. FaceInitTimer is not available in the library libFm_c. a.
	widget is the widget that will be used as "self" when the timer script is run.
	script is a string containing the script to execute. call_data is the value of
	the call_data ($) in the script. delay is the delay in milliseconds before the
	script is run. repeat if non-zero, is the delay in milliseconds between
	successive calls of the script after the initial delay.
	
	Scope: FACE scripts application 	
	
	The corresponding C function is: FaceInitTimer
	See also:
	        FaceStopTimer
	        XtAddTimeOut
	
	

init_timer
	Synopsis:
	        Timer init_timer( Widget w, String script, None call_data, Int delay, Boolean auto-repeat )
	
	Description:
	
	Initialize a timer so that the script script will be called automatically in
	delay milliseconds. script is a string containing a FACE script. After delay
	milliseconds, the script will be parsed and executed, using w as a reference
	Widget, and call_data as the $ argument. If auto-repeat is True, then the timer
	is re-initialized automatically after the script is executed, with the same
	delay. The return value is an identifier which can be passed to stop_timer to
	cancel the timer before it has expired. If you intend to generate C-code
	interfaces you should use the alternative functions: CallCallbacksTimeOut,
	GetActiveValueTimeOut or SetActiveValueTimeOut.
	
	Scope: FACE scripts only 	
	
	Example:
	
	In a pushbutton, set the label to 0 and increment it every half second as long
	as the button is armed. 
	
	armCallback = global t; 
	        global i;
	        i = 0; 
	        self:labelString = itoa ( i ) ; 
	        t = init_timer ( self, "global i; i = i+1; 
	                self:labelString = itoa ( i ) ;", 0, 500, True ) ;
	
	disarmCallback = global t; 
	        stop_timer ( t ) ; 
	
	

